==English==

===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:uder|extraordinary|tree=+}}
Abbreviation of {{m|en|extraordinary}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɛkstɹə/}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-extra.ogg|a=US}}
** {{audio|en|en-au-extra.ogg|a=AU}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-extra.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{hyphenation|en|ex|tra}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-,more}}

# {{lb|en|not comparable}} [[beyond|Beyond]] what is [[due]], [[usual]], [[expect]]ed, or [[necessary]]; [[extraneous]]; [[additional]]; [[supernumerary]].
#: {{ux|en|I don't mind doing some '''extra''' work, as long as I get '''extra''' pay.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2018|author=S. D. Tucker|chapter=Doctor Poolittle|title=Quacks! Dodgy Doctors and Foolish Fads Throughout History|page=147|publisher=[[w:Amberley Publishing|Amberley]]|location=w:Stroud, Gloucestershire|isbn=9781445671819|oclc=1032027057|passage=Kellogg himself became the biggest on-site celeb of all, delivering a weekly ‘Question Box’ lecture in which he explained that tobacco destroyed testicles, and that Ancient Rome had only fallen because the decadent Senators had started tossing their slaves into cookery pots to lend their food '''extra''' flavour, thus proving that an over-rich diet could lead to wholesale civilisational collapse.}}
# {{lb|en|not comparable|dated}} [[extraordinarily|Extraordinarily]] [[good]]; [[superior]].
# {{lb|en|comparable|slang}} [[over the top|Over the top]]; going beyond what is [[normal]] or [[appropriate]], often in a [[dramatic]] manner.
#: {{ux|en|You unfollowed her for posting cat memes? You're so '''extra'''!}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2017|author=Claire Craig|title=#Instabeauty|journal=Northern Woman|month=November|titleurl=https://issuu.com/graphics81/docs/northern_woman_november_2017|page=48
|passage=Shattered glass, pierced, bejewelled, chromed and glittered - nails are going totally '''extra''' on Insta at the minute and we approve.}}
#* {{see more citations|en}}

