===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Something [[additional]], such as an item above and beyond the ordinary [[school]] [[curriculum]], or added to the usual [[charge]] on a [[bill]].
#: {{syn|en|addition|supplement}}
# An extra edition of a [[newspaper]], which is printed outside of the normal printing cycle, for example to report an important late-breaking event.
#: {{ux|en|'''Extra''', '''extra'''! Read all about it!}}<!-- not sure if this is for the adj or the noun -->
# {{lb|en|cricket}} A [[run]] scored without the [[ball]] having [[hit]] the [[striker]]'s [[bat]] - a [[wide]], [[bye]], [[leg bye]] or [[no ball]].
#: {{synonyms|en|sundry}} <!--in Australia-->
# {{senseid|en|Q658371}}{{lb|en|acting}} A [[supernumerary]] or [[walk-on]] in a film or play.
# {{lb|en|slang}} The state or trait of being [[over the top]], of behaving in an overly [[dramatic]] manner.
#: {{ux|en|Stop! I can't deal with all your '''extra''' today!}}
# Something of an extra quality or grade. {{rfex|en}} <!--Webster 1913 supplement-->
# {{lb|en|Singapore|military|countable}} A day of extra [[duty|duties]] (often, over the weekends), as a form of [[punishment]].

